EFF Long Wordlist
=================

Work:    "EFF's New Wordlists for Random Passphrases" — eff_large_wordlist.txt
Author:  Electronic Frontier Foundation
Source:  https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2016/07/new-wordlists-random-passphrases
License: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 United States (CC BY 3.0 US)
         https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/us/

Used in Hespera as the word source for the hesplay phone remote's three-word
passphrase (cmd/hesplay/wordlist.go, compiled into the `hesplay` binary).

MODIFICATION NOTICE (required by CC BY 3.0 US section 4(b)): this is a
derivative of EFF's list. Its four hyphenated entries — drop-down, felt-tip,
t-shirt and yo-yo — have been removed, leaving 7,772 of the original 7,776
words. hesplay treats every non-letter as a word separator when normalising a
typed passphrase, so a hyphenated entry would make a three-word passphrase
normalise to four tokens. No words were added or altered.

